# Print sizes — all shirts

SKU source = always `Custom Label`. Helpers: `database/custom-label-database/support/Shirts Print Sizes.csv`, `Size References.csv`. BTC Product Data: `database/shared/btc_product_data/BTC_Product_Data.csv`.

Reverse fill (mock+UID only, blank-only mm, append missing keys): `python scripts/fill_size_references_from_cl.py --dry-run` then write. Custom Label `M123-45678` → Size References `M123 (45678)`. Do not dump non-mock SKUs. Do not use a generic mock prefix.

**Hoodies** (locked 2026-10-22): every row whose Gender Apparel contains `Hoodie` — kids, men, women — uses this square chart, not Shirts Print Sizes. Plain sweatshirts, tees, polos, and tanks stay on the shirt table. Women use the men band. Front and Back share the same mm. Kids also means `Youth` in Gender Apparel, or a kids age size (`3-4 Years`, `YXS`) even when Gender Apparel is only a style code. A size not on the chart maps to the nearest band; `6XL` does not map and is left alone. Applied on `Custom_Label_Database (Areeb).csv` (front and back slots only; pocket, sleeve, and corner slots stay).

| Band | XS | S | M | L | XL | 2XL | 3XL | 4XL | 5XL |
|------|----|---|---|---|----|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| Kids | 170×170 | 190×190 | 210×210 | 230×230 | 250×250 | — | — | — | — |
| Men / Women | — | 250×250 | 270×270 | 290×290 | 310×310 | 330×330 | 350×350 | 370×370 | 390×390 |

Kids ages: 3-4 Years and YXS → XS; 5-6 Years and YS → S; 7-8 Years and YM → M; 9-11 Years → L; 12-13, 12-14, 14-15 Years and Y2XL → XL. Adults: Extra Small, S, and `S (8-10)` → S; the same word or letter for M / L / XL / 2XL / 3XL / 4XL / 5XL, including `M (12-14)` through `5XL (34-36)`. `6XL` has no band.

**Presser** (locked 2026-10-22): actual platen 400×600 mm. Safe max used in the warehouse is **300×500** (W×H). Do not store a print wider than 300 or taller than 500. Adult hoodie 4XL (370×370) and 5XL (390×390) are over that width — flag them; do not silently shrink.

**All kinds of shirts** (t-shirt, tee, polo, sweatshirt, tank — and any row whose `Size` maps to the shirt table: Small/Medium/Large/YXS/12-13 Years, …), unless Gender Apparel is clearly not a shirt (hoodie, bag, tote, apron, beanie, hat, cap, iron-on, romper, sticker, mug, mask):

1. **Shirts Print Sizes.csv first** (Standard A4 for Front/Back; missing paper → A4). Size = DB `Size`, else PE `Size` via UID. Women use the men band.
2. **Then Size References.csv** if the band does not map, or for extra positions / paper / an **exact** `M## (UID)` row.

Pocket = 80×100. **Sleeve = 100×100** (locked 2026-10-23): any slot whose Position Name contains `sleeve` (`Sleeve`, `Right Sleeve`), blank slots included. Front and Back share the same mm. Position names come from DB `Print Positions`, not Size Ref suffixes. Applied on `Custom_Label_Database (Areeb).csv`.

**ISO paper A3–A6** (locked 2026-10-27): when the row is paper size A3 / A4 / A5 / A6 — not the shirt-table “Standard A4” band — Front Center / Back Center use ISO mm. Pocket stays 80×100; sleeve stays 100×100. Other positions stay. Detect in order: `Size` exact (`A4`) or paper token (`A5 15mm`, `A5-Rectangle`); then a dash token on `Custom Label` that is exactly `A3`/`A4`/`A5`/`A6` (a **leading** token only counts when Size/GA already shows paper, or Custom Label / Gender Apparel has iron-on / sticker / acrylic / photo / transfer — so `A3-F/B-…` and `A3-5000-…` stay garments); then a paper token in Gender Apparel. Applied on `Custom_Label_Database (Areeb).csv` via `scripts/rewrite_paper_sizes.py`.

| Paper | Front / Back Center |
|-------|---------------------|
| A6 | 105×148 |
| A5 | 148×210 |
| A4 | 210×297 |
| A3 | 297×420 |

**F8 / F8A** (locked 2026-10-20): a Custom Label with its own dash token `F8` or `F8A` is a pocket. `F80` is not. Single filled position → `Print Positions` and `Position 1 Name` = `Front Left Pocket`, **80×100**, kids included (the old kids 65×80 chart is retired).

**F/P-F8 and B4** (locked 2026-10-23): `F/P` together with `F8` is **Front Left Pocket** only, 80×100 — not Front Center plus a pocket. `B4` is **Back Center**. One cell can hold both tails (`F/P-F8-M-T-BLK-5XL 161121LG-B4-M-T-BLK-5XL`). Applied on `Custom_Label_Database (Areeb).csv`. `F/P` without `F8` stays Front Center plus Front Left Pocket.

**Default position when Custom Label has no position token** (locked 2026-10-28): no `F/P`/`F/B`/`F8`/`F4`/`B4`/`FP-`/leading `B-`/`P-` style code → **Front Center** only. Do not invent pocket/back from peer or mock stubs on Areeb. Exceptions locked same day: all `A3-B-M-T-*` → **Back Center** only; leave `ASV-*`, `FP-*`, `X97`/`x97`, `XZ8`, `X94`, `xz7` as-is; mock stubs / mock+UID follow **Mocks Database**. Areeb drift vs live Front Center restored via `scripts/fix_areeb_pos_from_live.py` (Areeb only).

**Not shirts:** Size References only. **Never** use a generic mock prefix (`M96` without this UID) — that wrongly gave `M96-138334` 318×450 instead of 250×353.

**W415 Jute Stuff Bag** (locked 2026-10-12): do not use the shirt table. Supervisor sizes are centimetres; store millimetres after subtracting 20 mm from each side. Applies to `W415-NAT-{size}-Yes` and the same garment (`BG-W415-NTRL-XXS`).

| Size | Given | Stored |
|------|-------|--------|
| XXS | 8×12 cm | 60×100 mm |
| XS | 12×16 cm | 100×140 mm |
| S | 18×22 cm | 160×200 mm |
| M | 25×28 cm | 230×260 mm |
| L | 34×40 cm | 320×380 mm |
| XL | 50×55 cm | 480×530 mm |

Fill **blank** Width/Height only, unless asked to correct wrong mm.

```text
python scripts/fill_from_seeds.py --steps print --shirts-only --w1-blank
```
